rnet banking, cash management, safe deposit boxes, direct deposit, automatic drafts, bill payment, and mobile banking services. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Greenville, South Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. R. Arthur Seaver Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $740,243 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 315 people. Revenue per employee of $375K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $95K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Southern First Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $575M market cap on $118M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $30M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.00\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (95% sell ratio, net $2.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (SFST) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_SFST_Edition_111326010601_1794593162.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794593162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (SFST) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/Understanding_the_Setup:_SFST_and_Scalable_Risk_110326012201_1793730121.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793730121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Comparison: Woori Bank (NYSE:WF) vs. Southern First Bancshares (NASDAQ:SFST)","source":"t